provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "example_bucket" {
  bucket = "example-bucket-${random_string.random_suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  tags = {
    Name        = "Example S3 Bucket"
    Environment = "Development"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" "example_bucket_ownership_controls" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.id

  rule {
    object_ownership = "BucketOwnerPreferred"
  }
}

resource "random_string" "random_suffix" {
  length = 8
  special = false
}
```

This Terraform program creates an AWS S3 bucket named `example-bucket-<random_suffix>` in the `us-west-2` region. It sets the bucket ACL to `private` and applies ownership controls to ensure that the bucket owner automatically owns and has full control over every object in the bucket. The bucket is tagged with `Name` and `Environment`. The `random_string` resource is used to generate a random suffix for the bucket name to ensure uniqueness.

